    <string name="auth_notice">Security Notice: We strongly recommend using an Alternate Vehicle Authorization sub-account (created via the official BYD app) with remote vehicle permissions rather than your primary owner account. Independent unofficial third-party app.</string>
    <string name="setup_guide_title">First-Time Setup Guide (2nd Account &amp; PIN)</string>
    <string name="setup_guide_subtitle">How to prepare a secondary BYD account before signing in</string>
    <string name="btn_show_guide">Show</string>
    <string name="btn_hide_guide">Hide</string>
    <string name="setup_guide_warning">Do NOT use your main owner account. Authorize a separate 2nd BYD account in the official BYD App instead — this protects your primary login, prevents forced logouts, and lets you revoke access anytime.</string>
    <string name="setup_guide_step1_title">1. Authorize a Secondary Email</string>
    <string name="setup_guide_step1_body">In the official BYD App on your primary owner account, go to My Car → Vehicle Authorization → Add Authorized Account. Enter a secondary email address and enable Remote Control permissions. The email does not need to be registered prior to authorization.</string>
    <string name="setup_guide_step2_title">2. Register the Secondary Account &amp; Set Password</string>
    <string name="setup_guide_step2_body">Sign out of the official BYD App and register or sign in with that secondary email in the same country/region as your vehicle. Ensure a login password is set under My → Settings → Account &amp; Security → Password (OTP-only accounts are not supported).</string>
    <string name="setup_guide_step3_title">3. Accept Authorization &amp; Set Operation PIN</string>
    <string name="setup_guide_step3_body">On the secondary account in the official BYD App, accept the vehicle authorization invite. Set a 6-digit Operation PIN under My → Settings → Account &amp; Security → Operation Password, then test Lock or AC once in the official app.</string>
    <string name="setup_guide_step4_title">4. Fetch VIN &amp; Save Credentials</string>
    <string name="setup_guide_step4_body">Select your Cloud Region below, enter the secondary account email, login password, and 6-digit Operation PIN. Tap Fetch VIN to verify your vehicle, then tap Save.</string>
